timestamp=2026-11-04T12:13:36.516Z level=INFO run=b7b1a579 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\nimport pandas as pd\nimport numpy as np\n\nstations = pd.read_csv('/app/dataset/stations.csv')\nreadings = pd.read_csv('/app/dataset/readings.csv')\nreadings['timestamp'] = pd.to_datetime(readings['timestamp'])\nreadings['current_reading'] = pd.to_numeric(readings['current_reading'], errors='coerce')\ndf = readings.merge(stations, on='station_id', how='left')\n\nw_r = pd.read_csv('/app/dataset/weather_readings.csv')\nw_r['timestamp'] = pd.to_datetime(w_r['timestamp'])\nweather_agg = w_r.groupby(['district', 'timestamp']).agg({\n    'temperature_c': 'mean',\n    'humidity_pct': 'mean',\n    'wind_speed_m_s': 'mean',\n    'rain_accumulation_mm': 'mean',\n}).reset_index()\ndf = df.merge(weather_agg, on=['district', 'timestamp'], how='left')\n\nts_map = {}\nmeta = {}\nfor sid, g in df.groupby('station_id'):\n    g = g.sort_values('timestamp').copy()\n    ts_map[sid] = g.set_index('timestamp')['current_reading']\n    meta[sid] = {'district': g['district'].iloc[0], 'pollutant': g['pollutant'].iloc[0]}\n\n# Also check ST050 (has many NaNs) - muted swings candidate? ST051 was most muted. ST050 has high missing count too.\n# But the task says \"faulty station set\" - pick 3. The clues map to 3 different types.\n# Clue 1 type (rhythm issue): ST020 fits - follows pattern broadly but different rhythm (direction flips). Also high diff in max vs lag0 correlation in some cases? Or just qualitative.\n# Clue 2 (muted swings): ST051 is top muted (ratio ~0.33). Others too, but ST051 is strongest.\n# Clue 3 (deviations align too neatly with one environmental driver): ST060 has highest resid correlation with rain (0.69). That’s notable.\n# These three (ST020, ST051, ST060) come from different districts/pollutants and match the three patterns.\n# Let us verify each against the exact clue description.\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
