timestamp=2026-11-04T12:13:50.008Z level=INFO run=b7b1a579 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="cat > /app/answer.py << 'PY'\ndef answer() -> set[str]:\n    # Based on analysis:\n    # 1. One problematic station broadly follows local patterns, but not with the same rhythm as its peers.\n    #    -> ST020 (PSIE_POLE, PM10): peer alignment poor in timing/rhythm; direction changes often misaligned with peers.\n    # 2. Another looks plausible point-by-point yet its swings are unusually muted compared with comparable local stations.\n    #    -> ST051 (FABRYCZNA, PM25): variance much lower than peer median (muted swings), plausible values.\n    # 3. A third appears ordinary in aggregate, but its remaining deviations line up a bit too neatly with one environmental driver.\n    #    -> ST060 (FABRYCZNA, PM10): residuals relative to peers show strong correlation with rain_accumulation_mm.\n    return {\"ST020\", \"ST051\", \"ST060\"}\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    import json\n    with open(\"/app/answer.json\", \"w\") as f:\n        json.dump(answer(), f, default=list)\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
